Rule 1 (reduction dim must be within valid range of input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 2 (for empty tensors, a valid reduction dim must be provided to avoid flattening with numel() == 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0 then ( (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1 )
>>
Rule 3 (negative dim indices must normalize to a valid non-negative dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 < 0 then 0 ≤ v_2 + ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2 + ndim(v_1) ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 4 (keepdim=true requires a valid reduction dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : bool} |= if v_3 = true then (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1)
>>
Rule 5 (valid dim choices for 1D input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then (v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = -1)
